---
// A Maxwell and a Burgers material letting go of a stress, under a slider:
// the Theory page's figure for the Burgers section.
---
<figure class="plot" id="relaxation">
  <div class="legend">
    <span class="item"><span class="swatch" style="border-top-color:#2a78d6"></span><span>Burgers, as in the model</span></span>
    <span class="item"><span class="swatch" style="border-top-color:#eb6834"></span><span>Maxwell, same steady viscosity</span></span>
  </div>
  <div data-timeline></div>
  <div data-chart class="chart"></div>
  <p data-note class="note-line">&nbsp;</p>
  <figcaption>
    <b>Two materials letting go.</b> Each is strained by a step and held; the
    curves are the fraction of the stress it still carries. The Burgers
    material drops by its transient at once, then crosses the Maxwell
    material and outlasts it.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<script>
  import { startRelaxation } from "../viz/relaxation";
  startRelaxation(document.getElementById("relaxation")!, import.meta.env.BASE_URL);
</script>
